---
import ProseLayout from '../layouts/ProseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../site.config';
---

<ProseLayout
  title="Cookie policy"
  description={`Which cookies and similar technologies ${site.name} uses, why, and how to control them.`}
  path="/cookie-policy/"
  updated="2026-09-25"
  lede="This page explains the cookies and similar technologies used on this site and how you can control them."
>
  <h2>What are cookies?</h2>
  <p>
    Cookies are small text files a website places on your device. Similar technologies include local storage and pixels. They
    can be <strong>first-party</strong> (set by the site you’re visiting) or <strong>third-party</strong> (set by another service,
    such as an advertising provider).
  </p>

  <h2>What we use</h2>
  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Examples</th><th>Can you refuse?</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Preference (local storage)</td>
          <td>Remembers whether you chose light or dark mode.</td>
          <td><code>theme</code></td>
          <td>Yes — clear site data in your browser; the site still works.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Advertising (Google AdSense)</td>
          <td>Serve and measure ads, limit how often you see an ad, detect fraud, and — with consent where required — personalize ads.</td>
          <td><code>__gads</code>, <code>__gpi</code>, <code>__eoi</code>, and Google cookies such as <code>IDE</code></td>
          <td>Yes — via the consent message, Google Ads Settings or your browser.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Consent</td>
          <td>Store your consent choices so the consent message isn’t shown on every page.</td>
          <td>IAB TCF consent string (e.g. <code>FCCDCF</code>)</td>
          <td>Needed to remember your choice.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    We don’t use cookies to read or store the numbers you enter in calculators — those never leave your browser. Exact cookie
    names used by Google can change over time; see
    <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/cookies" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Google’s cookie documentation</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>How to control cookies</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Consent message:</strong> visitors in the EEA, UK and Switzerland can accept or reject advertising cookies, and change their choice at any time through the privacy settings link.</li>
    <li><strong>Google Ads Settings:</strong> turn off personalized ads at <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">adssettings.google.com</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Industry opt-outs:</strong> <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">aboutads.info/choices</a> (U.S.) and <a href="https://www.youronlinechoices.eu/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">youronlinechoices.eu</a> (Europe).</li>
    <li><strong>Your browser:</strong> block or delete cookies in your browser settings. Blocking all cookies may affect how some sites work, but every calculator here works without them.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>More information</h2>
  <p>
    Read our <a href="/privacy-policy/">privacy policy</a> for more on how information is handled, or email
    <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> with questions.
  </p>
</ProseLayout>
